content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal leakage of about 1 drop per second (steady drip). This matches the troubleshooting symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4). The evidence gives no acceptable seal leakage rate, so the drip cannot be compared with a numeric limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing vibration is 2.1 mm/s. The applicable limit is Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual, measured on the bearing housings in mm/s RMS. The reading falls in Zone A (0.0 to 2.8 mm/s, 'New machines'), below the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary. It is well below the 4.5 mm/s 'Restricted - plan maintenance' boundary and the 7.1 mm/s 'Damage likely - stop the pump' boundary. The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading to be classified, but only the drive-end reading was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 66 C. The applicable limit is the manual specification table: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C, measured on the housing surface. The reading is within the normal range, 4 C below the normal upper limit and 14 C below alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: vibration and bearing temperature are normal, so there is no evidence of bearing distress. The only defect is the seal leak, which needs planned seal replacement but does not meet any documented stop criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical seal faces. This is the most likely cause, because vibration (Zone A) and bearing temperature (below 70 C) are both normal and so do not point to misalignment or bearing problems.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal has run dry at some point, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush from the pump discharge. The manual states the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is less likely given the low vibration, but it is listed as a cause of seal leakage and should be verified with a laser alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump and drain it. The line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite, so treat the drained liquid and any seal leakage as chemically dosed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment, because it weighs 68 kg. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and the impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve (HF3-455). Inspect the sleeve for scoring and replace it if it is scored (see open questions on the acceptance limit).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, check the drive-end (6312-C3) and non-drive-end (6310-C3) bearings. Replace both as a pair only if either shows wear or noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new component mechanical seal HF3-450 (not HF3-450B, because this serial is below HF3-22000). Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten all fasteners to manual Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): seal gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, and bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if disturbed. Do not use the 30 Nm gland torque from SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment, because removing the back pull-out assembly moves the bearing housing and alignment is a listed cause of seal leakage. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is in place. Fill and vent the pump before start-up and never run it dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, check that the seal is not leaking. Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3; Zone A (up to 2.8 mm/s) is expected. Confirm bearing housing temperature stays at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type (correct for serial below HF3-22000)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve - conditional, fit only if scoring is found on inspection; recommend having one available",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The filtered-water line, including pumps P-101 to P-106, is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat the leakage and the drained fluid as chemical exposure.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry. Confirm the Plan 11 flush and that the pump is fully primed before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians (8.0 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection finds bearing wear, add bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) replaces seal HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B. However, it applies only to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above, and states that pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450 and manual Table 5. P-102 is serial HF3-19870, which is below HF3-22000, so the manual applies and HF3-450 is the correct seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: the bulletin gives 30 Nm, but only for HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. For this pump (HF3-19870, seal HF3-450), manual Table 5 applies: M10 seal gland nuts at 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve replacement criterion: the 0.1 mm scoring-depth limit for sleeve HF3-455 appears only in the bulletin, which does not apply to this serial. The manual says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring and gives no depth limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What seal leakage rate is acceptable for the HF-300? The evidence gives no numeric limit, so it cannot say whether a drip of about 1 per second of hypochlorite-dosed water justifies an immediate stop rather than planned replacement.",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing housing vibration reading? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest classified, but only the drive-end value (2.1 mm/s) was reported.",
    "Was the 2.1 mm/s vibration reading taken as velocity RMS, as Figure 3 requires?",
    "What PPE and chemical handling or decontamination precautions apply to sodium hypochlorite? SSP-07 only states that the line is dosed.",
    "What scoring depth makes sleeve HF3-455 rejectable on pumps below serial HF3-22000? The manual gives no limit, and the bulletin's 0.1 mm limit covers only later serials.",
    "Does the HF3-450 component seal need sleeve measurement or a set-up dimension on installation? The bulletin implies the pre-set cartridge seal removes that step, but the manual procedure gives no values.",
    "Is the HF3-450 seal material compatible with sodium hypochlorite? This is not addressed in the evidence.",
    "Has the Plan 11 flush ever been lost, or has the pump run dry? This would help confirm the root cause.",
    "Are HF3-450, HF3-120 and HF3-455 in stock? Availability is not covered by the evidence."
  ]
}
